</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experimental Results</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sensitivity Analysis</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we investigate the impact of three key design factors of the proposed <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> model, which influence its computation cost and the effectiveness of using its capacity (which can be seen by measuring the performance on downstream tasks): 1) patch size <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>; 2) classification token construction strategy; and 3) training duration.
In addition, we evaluate these design choices to quantify their trade-offs in terms of computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>1 </span>Patch Size</h4>

<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE IV</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of different patch sizes <math id="S4.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> using linear probing. Performance is reported as <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">mAP</abbr> (%) for m-bigearthnet, <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">AA</abbr> (%) for m-brick-kiln, m-so2sat, and m-eurosat, and <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">IoU</abbr> (%) for m-cashew-plant and m-SA-crop-type.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Model</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;"><math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span><span id="S4.T4.5.1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;" colspan="4">Classification</td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;"></td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;" colspan="2">Segmentation</td>
<td id="S4.T4.5.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.5pt 3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T4.5.1.6.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="S4.T4.5.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="S4.T4.5.1.6.1.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S4.T4.5.1.6.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
