</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze the effect of patch size <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> on the performance and computational cost of the <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> model, we train four <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> variants with four different patch sizes <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\{14,16,28,32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\{14,16,28,32\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<a href="#S4.T4" title="In IV-A1 Patch Size ‣ IV-A Sensitivity Analysis ‣ IV Experimental Results ‣ CSMoE: An Efficient Remote Sensing Foundation Model with Soft Mixture-of-Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a> shows the downstream performance on the scene classification and semantic segmentation datasets as well as the computational requirements in terms of number of parameters, <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">FLOP</abbr> and <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">C2C</abbr> ratio for different patch sizes <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the table, one can see that <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> variants trained with smaller patch sizes (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\{14,16\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\{14,16\}</annotation></semantics></math>) outperform those using larger patch sizes (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\{28,32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\{28,32\}</annotation></semantics></math>) across all classification and segmentation tasks, with particularly large gains on the segmentation datasets m-cashew-plant and m-SA-crop-type.
For example, <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> with patch size <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=14</annotation></semantics></math> achieves 59.4% <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">IoU</abbr> and 39.8% <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">IoU</abbr>, compared to 46.0% and 35.8% for <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">CSMoE</abbr> with patch size <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=32</annotation></semantics></math>, on the m-cashew-plant and m-SA-crop-type datasets, respectively.
A possible explanation is that smaller patches retain finer spatial structures in the embeddings, which may be particularly beneficial for tasks requiring precise delineation of heterogeneous land-cover types.
However, this improvement comes with a substantial increase in <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">FLOP</abbr>, from 2.92B to 13.40B, and a corresponding drop in the <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">C2C</abbr> ratio from 94.86 to 20.22.
We observe that patch sizes of 14 or 16 offer the best trade-off between performance and compute, while larger patch sizes, though more efficient, lead to under-utilization of the model’s capacity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>2 </span>Classification Token Construction Strategy</h4>

